{"record":{"id":"REQ-RUN-0327","title":"Paired stores use the same schema or a similar schema","status":"Draft","version":"1.0.0","created":"2026-10-25","last_updated":"2026-10-25","owner":"randlee","supersedes":null,"superseded_by":null,"requirement_statement":{"text":"Definitions: A consumer repository is an application project using the framework. A store holds one database engine's rows and SQL. A copy adaptor pairs local SQLite with the remote schema; a host-aggregate adaptor pairs host SQLite with a remote aggregate. SQL means Structured Query Language. The statements below remain subject to the explicit deferral in this record. In the copy pattern, both stores have the same schema. In the host-aggregate pattern, tables or columns may exist on only one side, as specified by this record's success criterion.

This record is deferred and does not apply to Phase D; it creates no implementation or validation obligation until reopened.

Synchronization between databases is deferred. This requirement binds nothing until it is taken up again.","statements":[{"modal":"Must","text":"In the copy pattern, generation MUST produce the same schema on both stores."},{"modal":"Must","text":"In the host-aggregate pattern, generation MUST support tables present on only one side."},{"modal":"Must","text":"In the host-aggregate pattern, generation MUST support columns present on only one side."}]},"rationale":"One SQL string executed on both engines was rejected: each engine has its own SQL, and the schemas are the same or similar (ADR-RUN-0305). Owner, 2026-10-25 (ADR-RUN-0305): the storage plan is a generated adaptor in the consumer repository.","success_criteria":{"text":"1. The copy pattern generates the same schema on both stores. The host-aggregate pattern generates a similar schema, with tables or columns that exist on only one side.","acceptance_criteria":[],"test_evidence":[]},"dependencies":{"text":"","requires":[],"related":[]},"product_applicability":{"text":"","applies_to":[],"does_not_apply_to":[]},"implementation_notes":{"text":"","key_considerations":[]},"test_strategy":{"text":"","test_types":[]},"related_documents":{"text":"","requirements":[],"architecture_decisions":[],"design_documents":[],"work_items":[],"external_references":[]}}}
